"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fd8a8ee/content/data/versions/632.json", "paragraphs": ["Emergency Lawyers is a rights group in Khartoum, Sudan's capital. It said jets attacked miners on Saturday. The miners worked at gold sites in River Nile state. The group said the number of dead may still grow.", "A newspaper called Sudan Tribune reported more deaths. A survivor said many more people were hurt. Witnesses said the attack started around 6 in the morning. Planes fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps.", "Egypt has faced similar accusations before. In June, Sudan's leaders said they would investigate earlier strikes. Gold is at the center of these border problems. Sudan's civil war has led more people to mine gold without permission."], "paragraphs_zh": ["“紧急律师”是苏丹首都喀土穆的一家人权组织。该组织说，战机在周六袭击了矿工。这些矿工在尼罗河州的淘金点工作。该组织表示，死亡人数可能还会上升。", "《苏丹论坛报》报道说，死亡人数更多。一名幸存者说，还有更多人受伤。目击者说，袭击大约在早上6点开始。飞机向矿工的营地发射了五枚以上导弹。", "埃及以前也面临过类似指控。今年6月，苏丹领导人说将调查之前的袭击。黄金是这些边境问题的核心。苏丹内战让更多人未经许可去淘金。"], "body": "Emergency Lawyers is a rights group in Khartoum, Sudan's capital. It said jets attacked miners on Saturday. The miners worked at gold sites in River Nile state. The group said the number of dead may still grow.\n\nA newspaper called Sudan Tribune reported more deaths. A survivor said many more people were hurt. Witnesses said the attack started around 6 in the morning. Planes fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps.\n\nEgypt has faced similar accusations before. In June, Sudan's leaders said they would investigate earlier strikes. Gold is at the center of these border problems. Sudan's civil war has led more people to mine gold without permission.", "body_zh": "“紧急律师”是苏丹首都喀土穆的一家人权组织。该组织说，战机在周六袭击了矿工。这些矿工在尼罗河州的淘金点工作。该组织表示，死亡人数可能还会上升。\n\n《苏丹论坛报》报道说，死亡人数更多。一名幸存者说，还有更多人受伤。目击者说，袭击大约在早上6点开始。飞机向矿工的营地发射了五枚以上导弹。\n\n埃及以前也面临过类似指控。今年6月，苏丹领导人说将调查之前的袭击。黄金是这些边境问题的核心。苏丹内战让更多人未经许可去淘金。", "text": "Emergency Lawyers is a rights group in Khartoum, Sudan's capital. It said jets attacked miners on Saturday. The miners worked at gold sites in River Nile state. The group said the number of dead may still grow. A newspaper called Sudan Tribune reported more deaths. A survivor said many more people were hurt. Witnesses said the attack started around 6 in the morning. Planes fired more than five missiles at the miners' camps. Egypt has faced similar accusations before. In June, Sudan's leaders said they would investigate earlier strikes. Gold is at the center of these border problems. Sudan's civil war has led more people to mine gold without permission.", "vocab": [{"word": "strike", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空袭；打击", "note": "这里指飞机攻击", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "miner", "pos": "noun", "zh": "矿工；淘金者", "note": "找金子或挖矿的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rights group", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "人权组织", "note": "为人们争取权利的组织", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "border", "pos": "noun", "zh": "边境；边界", "note": "两个国家之间的线", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "kill", "pos": "verb", "zh": "杀死", "note": "过去式是 killed", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "attack", "pos": "noun/verb", "zh": "袭击；攻击", "note": "用武力打别人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "witness", "pos": "noun", "zh": "目击者", "note": "看到事情发生的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "gold", "pos": "noun", "zh": "黄金；金子", "note": "一种黄色的贵金属", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says", "summary_original": "Neither Egypt nor Sudan has commented on the alleged strikes on an artisanal mining camp on Saturday.", "body_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says\nBy\nAleks Phillips\nPublished\n3 hours ago\nAt least 72 civilians who had been prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, a regional rights group says.\nEmergency Lawyers, based in the Sudanese capital, Khartoum, said jets targeted the so-called artisanal miners at a popular gold mining sites in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday.\nNeither the Egyptian government nor the de facto Sudanese authorities have so far commented.\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illicit activity along its southern border.\nEmergency Lawyers noted the previous alleged attacks and said they represented not only a violation of Sudan's sovereign territory but demonstrated the government's lack of control over the region.\n\"The deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians violates international humanitarian law and the right to life,\" it said in a statement on Sunday. \"These acts may constitute war crimes.\"\nIt noted that its death toll was provisional and could rise.\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could far exceed the number reported by Emergency Lawyers, citing a survivor of Saturday's attack who said many more people had been injured.\nEyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time (04:00 GMT), with the aircraft firing more than five missiles directly at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside, the newspaper wrote.\nThe Sudan Tribune reported claims in June that Egyptian forces had used drones and artillery to target artisanal mining sites in the same region, killing several, after sporadic incidents of Egyptian border guards of burning equipment, torching temporary shelters, and firing live ammunition to disperse mine workers.\nDays later, Egypt's border agency announced that it and the military had begun a sweeping security campaign along the border to foil illegal migration, drug smuggling and illegal mining.\nAt the same time, Sudan's de facto leader announced an investigation into the alleged strikes, which were said to have killed dozens.\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions.\nSudan's ongoing civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining - an often risky practice conducted by civilians with rudimentary tools and without official permission - particularly in remote areas near its borders.\nGold-rich areas such as those in River Nile state lie along porous borders in terrain historically associated with cross-border smuggling routes, with artisanally mined gold potentially feeding into those channels.\nEgypt's border force said in June that it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore along with amateur prospecting equipment.\nArtisanal mining has also reportedly continued in Sudan's conflict zones and smuggled gold may be a source of income for armed insurgent groups.\nThis has raised concerns of illicit Sudanese gold undermining the legitimate Egyptian gold market.\nRelated topics\nSudan\nEgypt\nAfrica\nMining\nMore on this story\nA simple guide to what is happening in Sudan\nPublished\n13 November 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:48:50.607058", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Emergency", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.737, "sm": 100, "em": 737, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Lawyers", "s": 0.75, "e": 1.163, "sm": 750, "em": 1162, "cs": 10, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "is", "s": 1.175, "e": 1.288, "sm": 1175, "em": 1287, "cs": 18, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.3, "e": 1.363, "sm": 1300, "em": 1362, "cs": 21, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "rights", "s": 1.375, "e": 1.712, "sm": 1375, "em": 1712, "cs": 23, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "group", "s": 1.725, "e": 1.988, "sm": 1725, "em": 1987, "cs": 30, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "in", "s": 2.0, "e": 2.125, "sm": 2000, "em": 2125, "cs": 36, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "Khartoum", "s": 2.138, "e": 2.763, "sm": 2137, "em": 2762, "cs": 39, "ce": 47, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": ",", "s": 2.763, "e": 2.987, "sm": 2762, "em": 2987, "cs": 47, "ce": 48, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "Sudan's", "s": 2.987, "e": 3.45, "sm": 2987, "em": 3449, "cs": 49, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "capital", "s": 3.462, "e": 4.013, "sm": 3462, "em": 4012, "cs": 57, "ce": 64, "si": 0}, 